; DOMAIN: homological-algebra/sheaf-cohomology [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: For a sheaf F of abelian groups on a topological space X, sheaf cohomology H^n(X,F) is the n-th right-derived functor of the global-sections functor Gamma(X,-)=F->F(X), computed from an injective (or acyclic, e.g. flasque) resolution 0->F->I^* and taking cohomology of Gamma(X,I^*). H^0(X,F)=F(X)=global sections. A short exact sequence of sheaves 0->F'->F->F''->0 yields a long exact sequence in cohomology. On a paracompact/nice space, Cech cohomology Hcheck^n(X,F) agrees with derived-functor H^n(X,F), and the Cech-to-derived spectral sequence relates them in general. de Rham/Dolbeault theorems are instances: H^n(X,R)=H^n_dR(X) via the acyclic resolution by smooth forms (Poincare lemma). Cohomology vanishes above the covering dimension (Grothendieck vanishing) and on flasque/soft/fine sheaves in positive degree.
; Structure: (H^n(X,F)=R^n Gamma(X,-), injective/flasque/acyclic resolution + cohomology of global sections) (H^0=Gamma(X,F)=global sections) (LES from SES of sheaves) (Cech = derived-functor on paracompact; Cech-to-derived spectral sequence in general) (de Rham/Dolbeault via acyclic resolutions) (flasque/soft/fine => higher cohomology vanishes).
; Result: sheaf cohomology measures the global obstruction to passing from local sections to global ones; H^0 gives global sections and higher H^n encode gluing/extension obstructions, unifying Cech, de Rham, and Dolbeault theories under the derived-functor formalism.
; Bridge: genesis_ext_tor (H^n(X,F) is R^n of the left-exact Gamma, exactly the derived-functor pattern of Ext; computed via acyclic resolutions) + genesis_spectral_sequence (Cech-to-derived spectral sequence, and the Leray spectral sequence H^p(Y,R^q f_* F)=>H^{p+q}(X,F) for a map f:X->Y) + genesis_de_rham (de Rham theorem H^n(X,R)=H^n_dR(X) is sheaf cohomology via the acyclic smooth-form resolution) + genesis_group_cohomology (H^n(G,M)=H^n(BG;M_loc) is sheaf/local-system cohomology of the classifying space).
(= (sheaf-cohomology $X $F $n) (cohomology (global-sections (acyclic-resolution $F)) $n))
(= (sheaf-cohomology $X $F 0) (global-sections $X $F))
(= (flasque-acyclic $F) (= (sheaf-cohomology $X $F (succ $n)) 0))
(= (cech-equals-derived $X $F) (paracompact $X))
(= (leray-ss $f $F) (=> (E2 (sheaf-cohomology (codomain $f) (higher-direct-image $f $F))) (sheaf-cohomology (domain $f) $F)))
(= (de-rham-instance $X) (= (sheaf-cohomology $X reals $n) (de-rham-cohomology $X $n)))